    title: 'Deutsch-Jozsa, Grover, and Shor',
    description: 'Master three landmark quantum algorithms that demonstrate exponential and quadratic speedups over classical approaches for search, verification, and factoring.',
    prerequisites: ['Topics 1-2: qubit states, gates, measurement, superposition, and entanglement', 'Classical complexity theory (P, NP, exponential time)', 'Modular arithmetic basics (for Shor\\\'s algorithm)', 'Oracle/black-box model of computation'],
