    numericalExample: 'VQE for H2 molecule: the Hamiltonian has 4 Pauli terms: H = -0.81I + 0.17Z_0 - 0.22Z_1 + 0.18X_0X_1 + 0.18Y_0Y_1. With a 2-qubit ansatz |\\\\psi(\\\\theta)\\\\rangle = RY(\\\\theta_1)|00\\\\rangle -> CNOT -> RY(\\\\theta_2) -> CNOT, we measure each Pauli term for different \\\\theta values. At \\\\theta_1 = 0.7, \\\\theta_2 = 1.2: <I> = 1.0, <Z_0> = 0.3, <Z_1> = -0.5, <X_0X_1> = 0.8, <Y_0Y_1> = 0.7. Total energy: C = -0.81(1.0) + 0.17(0.3) + (-0.22)(-0.5) + 0.18(0.8) + 0.18(0.7) = -0.81 + 0.051 + 0.11 + 0.144 + 0.126 = -0.379. The exact ground state energy of H2 is -1.137 Hartree (using a minimal basis). After 50 optimization iterations with COBYLA, the VQE converges to -1.127 Hartree, achieving chemical accuracy (error < 1.6 mHartree). The classical optimizer needed ~200 circuit evaluations, each requiring 1000 measurement shots.',
